data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"With $p = \\sigma(m)$: the gradient is $p - y$ and the Hessian is $p(1-p)$. For a large positive margin $e^{-m}$ is tiny, and for a large negative margin $e^{m}$ is tiny. So write the sigmoid in terms of $z = e^{-|m|}$, which can never overflow, and choose the branch that matches the sign of $m$."},"hints_note":null}

